{
  "kind": "tea",
  "teaId": "bleeding-woman",
  "text": "Twelve years of bleeding, every doctor paid, and Mark says she was nothing bettered, but rather grew worse.\n\nThat's the text. Not my summary. Mark writes that she suffered many things of many physicians and spent all that she had, and got worse.\n\nTwelve years. Broke. Out of options.\n\nSo she hears about Jesus, and she does not go to the front and ask. She comes up behind him in a crowd, because she says within herself, \"If I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole.\"\n\nAnd she does. And immediately it stops.\n\nShe could have walked. That was the plan. Get in, get out, nobody knows.\n\nAnd he stops the entire procession.\n\nIn a crowd pressing on him from every side he turns around and says, \"Who touched my clothes?\" And the disciples basically tell him that's an insane question. Look at this crowd.\n\nHe keeps looking.\n\nSo she comes fearing and trembling, falls down, and tells him all the truth. Not a summary. All of it.\n\nAnd he says, \"Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole. Go in peace.\"\n\nDaughter. In front of everybody.\n\nHe wouldn't let her leave as a secret.",
